      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{62845dc19646c60b7bdbb3d0|full_name}\n\nIt would be good not just for not breaking an avatar, but also something that perhaps doesnt relate to looks. say avatars have accessibility features, or performance toggles that have save checked, meaning all those would also be saved with your \"look\".\n\nAs annoying as it only working on new avatars having to update the SDK to have an extra box, it means it would not both get in the way, or break avatars, which for any big update is something VRChat wants to avoid asap.\n\nIt's not too big of a change, and VRChat often updates the SDK every couple months or so, even adding new stuff to the Toon Standered shaider last patch ^o^   \n\nI have avatars with my own save systems I've implemented onto them, and half the toggles would be VERY annoying if they saved with the save system, so I make sure to not put those toggles (That have \"saved\" checked on in parameters still). But since Looks would act in a way like an avatar load out save system, again having a lot of general prop and such toggles save with your \"look\" would get in the way, again allong with breaking a lotta avatars and prefabs due to how they design the backend to work with peramiter drivers and save checked on / off.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
    {
      "_id": "6a95ddc04164b74953ad1954",
