      },
      "restoredAt": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Hey, I know this feedback request is probably looked at as a niche \"nice to have\"/low priority feature, but I'd like to bring more attention to this request as it absolutely could be huge for reducing animator load and/or alleviate users needing background OSC apps to accomplish custom toggle presets. It would also bring even more attention to VRC Accessories since that's what Looks are centered around!\n\nCurrently, a common way avatar creators create these \"custom save presets\" is by using hundreds of Parameter Drivers in the animator to copy and load the desired params.\n\nAs an example, here's one of my private avatar IDs that has this tech: avtr_db31f76f-cf49-4acd-abfd-7e9a16e7e034\n\nAlso here's a rough example screenshot of the UI where this checkbox could be opt-in when creating the avatar Look.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2026-03-18T01:22:22.209Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Since we now have a looks system for saving presets for avatar accessories, it would be an excellent opportunity to extend this feature to cover the much-requested feature of saving avatar parameter presets. \n\nAs an example: Editing a look should show the avatar in it current state (instead of the default as it does now) or perhaps there should be a button to sync the state to match how it is in game. Saving the look should save all saved parameters to the look. And loading a look should restore all saved parameters to those saved values, along with the attached accessories. \n\nThis would also solve the issue of default-disabled transforms not showing up in the looks editor.\n\nThis would be a big boon especially to marketplace avatars, who currently have to implement complex animator systems to provide save slots.",
